    "created_at": "2018-09-16T08:25:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-16T08:25:11Z",
    "body": "No Edge is (most) correct. I now understand how this interacts with this rule:\r\n\r\n> For the purpose of computing the block size, if it is not 'auto', the space allocated for the rendered legend that spills out past the border, if any, is expected to be substracted from the block size.\r\n\r\nI've added this:\r\n\r\n> If the content block-size would be negative, let the content block-size be zero instead.\r\n\r\nI think Edge is still wrong in where the placement of the fieldset/legend. It ought to still be centered over the fieldset's top border.",
